# Story 20: Background Bash (45s)
# Hook: Run long commands in the background. Check on them whenever you want.
# Duration: 45s
# Source: story-20-background-bash.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 8

[00:00.0 --> 00:04.0]
Start rysh -- you land in shell mode.

[00:04.0 --> 00:08.0]
Double-press Escape to enter prompt mode.

[00:08.0 --> 00:18.0]
Ask the AI to run a long-running command in the background. It won't block your terminal.

[00:18.0 --> 00:23.0]
While the command runs, you keep working. Check the output whenever you want.

[00:23.0 --> 00:30.0]
The AI retrieves the output from the background session.

[00:30.0 --> 00:38.0]
List all background sessions to see what's running.

[00:38.0 --> 00:42.0]
Every background session is tracked -- you never lose track of running tasks.

[00:42.0 --> 00:45.0]
Background bash -- fire and forget, check anytime.

